                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Public Health Microbiology is a specialized course offered by the School of Public Health at Fudan University. It focuses on the distribution, detection, and control of microorganisms in various environments such as water, soil, air, food, and healthcare settings. The curriculum covers microbial ecology, laboratory biosafety, indicator microorganisms, and detection methodologies. Emphasizing both theory and practice, the course equips students with essential skills to address microbiological challenges in public health.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
